export anchor CircuitBoardStyle:
    number: 126
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Circuit board
    idea: The dashboard laid out as a light green circuit board, with numbers on chips, projects as dashed component footprints carrying LED bar graphs, activity as test points on a trace, and the chart built from stacked copper pads.
    base: light
    palette:
        solderMask: #e4efe0, the board, with a #d3e4cd 32px grid
        componentBody: #f7faf4, fields, footprints and the style sheet
        silkscreen: #163521, main text and outlines
        silkMuted: #3c5c45, designators, meta and dashed courtyards
        trace: #9cc396, 4px traces and section rules, never text
        copper: #b8732f, pads, vias and mounting rings
        tinnedPad: #d39a5c, chart pads and the primary switch
        chip: #26302a, chip bodies, the nav pin header and the LED bar housing
        ledGreen: #7fe08e, lit LED segments on dark only
        onTrack: #1d7337, the ring LED
        atRisk: #8f4f00, the triangle LED
        behind: #b42318, the square LED, overdue and the alarm chip edge
    type:
        One monospace stack, ui-monospace, SF Mono, Cascadia Mono, Roboto
        Mono, Menlo, Consolas, monospace. The greeting is 34px 700, chip
        values 40px 700, section labels 15px 700 caps tracked 0.14em,
        project names 16px 700, body 14px at 1.5, designators and meta 12px
        caps tracked 0.1em.
    layout:
        One board up to 1280px with 14px corners, a 32px faint grid and
        copper ringed mounting holes in each corner. The header has a chip
        logo, the spaced caps brand with PCB-01 REV 2026.10 under it, a slot
        search, a tactile switch New project button with a round black cap, a
        round black buzzer for notifications and a U0 chip tag with the name.
        The nav is a dark pin header labelled J1, each link a pad and label,
        the current Home a lit copper pad. Horizontal traces with two vias
        divide sections. The greeting sits in silkscreen text with the date
        in spaced caps, and a boxed LED reads D1, 4 tasks are overdue. Four
        dark DIP chips labelled U1 to U4 hold the numbers, with grey pin legs
        above and below, the overdue chip edged in red. Projects are six
        dashed footprints labelled R1 to R6 in two columns, each with the
        name and team, a ten segment LED bar lit by tens of percent, the
        percent, tasks and due date, and a boxed status LED. Beside them,
        activity runs down a green trace as test points TP1 to TP6 with a
        copper pad, a dark tag, the sentence and the time. The chart is a
        panel of stacked copper pads, one pad per task, with values above,
        dates below and LAST WK = 59 and THIS WK = 73 over the two halves.
        Below 1000px chips go two by two and columns stack, below 640px the
        board loses its frame and footprints go single file.
    spacing: An 8px unit on a 32px board grid. 16px between footprints, 24px between chips, traces between sections.
    density: Medium dense, like a populated board, with two columns of modules beside a test point rail.
    corners: 14px on the board, 6px footprints, 2 to 4px chips and controls, round pads and holes.
    borders: 1.5px silkscreen lines, dashed courtyards round modules and 4px trace rules.
    shadows: Only a glow on lit LED segments and the board edge ring. Nothing floats.
    icons:
        Solid 16px LEDs with a hole punched in, a ring for On track, a
        triangle with a bar for At risk and a square with a square hole for
        Behind, always with the caps word in a bordered tag. Pads, vias and
        pins are ornament.
    focus: A 2px dashed silkscreen outline offset 3px with a 6px soft copper halo.
    tone: Terse engineering labels in caps, such as U1, R3, TP2, D1 and LAST WK = 59.
